    "description": "\"Urban Evader\" Adjustable Carbine Buttstock: Laffs Dynamics\n\nAn adjustable buttstock for use on AR-15 buffer tube extensions. Compact in overall size; designed for use with short \nbarrel carbines. The buttstock toe is angled to allow for ease of transitioning from low ready, to shouldering the \nweapon. Has a single 32mm long vertical sling loop. The latch lever has ridges down behind the pivot point for use \nin wet environments. \n\n\nThis buttstock is designed for Milspec Carbine Buffer Tubes only. \n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 220C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .20mm \nStandard Layer Height: .2mm\nWall Perimeters: 6+\nInfill: 25%+\nInfill Pattern: Gyroid\nMaterial Flow: 100%\nSupport Material Percentage: 16%\n\n\n\nHardware Needed:\n\n1x Compression Spring 3/8in x 3/4in\n\n1x M3x20 Set Screw / 3mm x 20mm Roll Pin\n\n\n\nAccreditations:\n\nProSpaceDog: Created similar locking latch geometry from his adjustable buttstock design. ",
